  "result": "Perfect! I've created the customer statements module:\n\n**src/statements.js** \u2014 Added:\n- **statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)** \u2014 Generates a customer billing statement:\n  - Validates customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if unknown)\n  - Filters invoices by:\n    - Customer ID (normalized)\n    - Status: 'issued' or 'partially_paid' only\n    - issueDate on or before asOf date\n  - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n  - Each invoice includes: number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due\n  - Sorted by issueDate ascending\n  - totalDue is sum of all due amounts\n\n**Key design:**\n- Normalizes customer ID for matching\n- Filters on status (excludes draft and paid)\n- Date cutoff is inclusive (asOf date included)\n- Calculates individual due amounts using balanceDue()\n- Sums totals for statement balance\n\nAdded 15 tests covering:\n- Basic statement generation\n- Date filtering (before, on, after asOf)\n- Status filtering (issued, partially_paid, excluding draft and paid)\n- Customer filtering\n- Sorting by date\n- Correct total/due calculation\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Error handling\n- Empty result sets\n\nAll 171 tests pass.",
